    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offensive engine today is powered heavily by favorable matchups against mediocre arms, headlined by **Kyle Tucker** (81.11) and **Andy Pages** (74.84). Both benefit from a prime opportunity against Merrill Kelly, whose xERA of 5.13 allows our outfield depth to reach elite efficiency. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.10) also grades out as a top-tier start; despite a moderate rain risk, he holds a significant platoon advantage against Tyler Mahle, and his aggressive base-running profile remains a priority as we hunt for scarcity in the stolen base category. **Jackson Merrill** (68.15) rounds out a high-upside outfield stack, buoyed by a strong dynamic platoon adjustment despite facing the tougher Ronel Blanco.\n\nWhile **Nasim Nunez** (66.19) provides a solid floor, the most interesting bench decision centers on **Luis Lara** (48.47). He narrowly missed the starting cut due to the sheer density of higher-projected hitters in our lineup today; while his switch-hitting versatility is a plus, the optimizer preferred the superior matchup data for **Jorge Polanco** and the high-order positioning of our middle-of-the-pack starters. **Coby Mayo** (38.03) fell further behind, largely hampered by a difficult matchup against Eovaldi and his currently uncertain position in the lineup. \n\nWe are monitoring several situational risks as we approach first pitch. **Drake Baldwin** (58.80), **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.10), **Jorge Polanco** (50.23), and **Heliot Ramos** (60.45) are all tethered to games with a 38-40% rain risk, which could shorten their appearances or impact efficiency. Additionally, **Gunnar Henderson** (61.95) must navigate the elite control of Eovaldi; while his platoon edge is significant, the veteran pitcher's ability to hold runners to a 42% stolen base success rate creates a minor drag on **Gunnar Henderson**\u2019s total scoring potential today. We are proceeding with our current lineup configuration to maximize both plate appearances and potential SB opportunities.",
